# Firmware files reviewed as open (source and licence known) for a Cubie A7A
# image (fedora/image-firmware.py).
#
# One shell-style glob per line, relative to the firmware directory
# (/usr/lib/firmware), matched with and without a .xz/.zst suffix; text after
# '#' is a comment. "image-firmware.py audit" (run by mkdevcard.sh, and
# "make audit-firmware IMG=...") reports every other file under the kernel's
# firmware paths as closed or unreviewed, Realtek firmware (rtl_nic, rtl_bt,
# rtlwifi, rtw88, rtw89, realtek, any rtl*/rtw*/rtk* name) separately and
# even when a line here would match: the script refuses such a line. The
# audit is a report: the image keeps linux-firmware and realtek-firmware, and
# a closed file is replaced only once an open one reaches parity.
#
# Add a line only with the driver that requests the file and the file's
# licence and source. Closed firmware does not go here.
#
# Closed pieces the board uses today (open replacement in progress):
# - rtl_nic/rtl8125b-2.fw (linux-firmware): Realtek's PHY patch for the Dual
#   2.5G Router HAT's RTL8125B ports. r8169 also runs without it (it warns and
#   continues; 1G links may be less stable).
# - powervr/*: Imagination's GPU firmware.
# - esm.fex: the HDMI HDCP 2.x engine firmware sunxidrm asks for; HDCP 2.x
#   stays off.
# - aic/aic8800d80/* (linux-firmware, LICENSE.aic): AICSemi's AIC8800D80
#   Wi-Fi/Bluetooth firmware, which cubie-a7a-aic8800-usb uses (Fedora's
#   firmware, replacing the user opt-in;
#   fedora/WIFI-FIRMWARE.md). Its Wi-Fi image is the SDIO build, which the
#   driver refuses for the A7A's USB chip until a USB build is there. No open
#   replacement exists.
# Not on the card: aic8800_fw/* (the optional user-installed USB override,
# cubie-a7a-wifi-firmware; never in an image).

# cfg80211 regulatory database (wireless-regdb, ISC licence, data rather than
# code; signed by the wireless-regdb maintainers). Installed only with the
# Wi-Fi driver package (cubie-a7a-aic8800-usb).
regulatory.db
regulatory.db.p7s
